Z||000000||MontanaFiero||07-04-2001||01:57 AM||||First--- Hi I''m back, <BR>Second-- <B>I'm finally getting the</B> (work on my) <B>Fiero bug.</B>  I am putting the front end together on my '86 SE, and the ball joints have got me stumped. When I did the ball joints on my '87 last fall, they mounted from the <I>top</I>, and the pictures in the CHILTON guide & the HAYES guide both show the ball joints on the top of the control arm.&gt;&gt;&gt; SO, I go out to my '86 and <B>GEE</B>, they <I>aren't</I> mounted from the top. They seem to be mounted <I>under</I> the upper control arm. The ones I got from Checker look like they are supposed to mount from the top.  What do I do? which is correct? part numbers would be nice too.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||RossT||07-04-2001||02:02 AM||||Can't help you, but I was wondering where the heck you've been???  Been a while..||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||07-04-2001||02:12 AM||||Are the joints bolted in?  If they are, they've been replaced at one time.  They are original if they are rivited, which would mean someone on the assembly line goofed (which I doubt).<P>My guess is someone or a shop wasn't thinking and bolted them in wrong.  I'd make sure the mounting surface didn't get warped, flatten it out if it needs to be and then drop the joints in like they should be.||||reg||1
Z||000003||MontanaFiero||07-04-2001||02:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RossT:<BR><B>Can't help you, but I was wondering where the heck you've been???  Been a while..</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><I>Well</I>.... I kinda ran a little low on funds and my hobbies had to suffer. (the fiero restoration and the internet). Now I am ready to rock and roll, and I am working lots of overtime. I <I>really</I> want to get that 3.4 liter I've been looking at for the past year.<P>As for the ball joints being in backwards, is that really possible?!?!  I just got rid of my parts car&gt;&gt;&gt;sure hope I don't need upper control arms.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
